bds 5,1 "Position report coarse"
date 2026-10-14
preamble
    Three-dimensional position report at coarse resolution. Intended to be
    read together with BDS 5,2, which carries the fine position offset and
    the figure of merit / data source.
    Source: EUROCONTROL, Mode-S Specific Services and Data Link Test Bench,
    "BDS 5,1 Position Report Coarse" (Mode S Specific Service Format).

    Coding: the sign bit is the most significant bit of a two's complement
    value spanning the whole sign+magnitude field, so a set sign bit yields
    magnitude - 2**(magnitude bits). This reproduces the ranges quoted in
    the tables (for example 19+1 bits at 360/1048576 deg gives +/-180 deg).

items

    STATUS "Status"
        definition
            Validity of the report.
        element 1
            table
                0: Invalid
                1: Valid
        remark
            Single status bit covering latitude, longitude and altitude.
            Set to 0 if any of the three parameters are invalid. Identical
            to the status bit in BDS 5,2.

    LAT_SIGN "Latitude Sign"
        definition
            Hemisphere of the latitude.
        element 1
            table
                0: North
                1: South
        remark
            Combined with LAT into a single signed value.

    LAT "Latitude"
        definition
            Aircraft latitude.
        element 19
            unsigned quantity 360/1048576 "°"
        remark
            Combined with LAT_SIGN into a single signed value.
            Coded with an MSB of 90 degrees so that the same coding
            algorithm applies as for longitude; the required valid range
            is +90 to -90 degrees.

    LON_SIGN "Longitude Sign"
        definition
            Hemisphere of the longitude.
        element 1
            table
                0: East
                1: West
        remark
            Combined with LON into a single signed value.

    LON "Longitude"
        definition
            Aircraft longitude.
        element 19
            unsigned quantity 360/1048576 "°"
        remark
            Combined with LON_SIGN into a single signed value.

    ALT_SIGN "Altitude Sign"
        definition
            Sign of the altitude.
        element 1
            table
                0: Positive
                1: Negative
        remark
            Combined with ALT into a single signed value.

    ALT "Pressure Altitude"
        definition
            Pressure altitude of the aircraft.
        element 14
            unsigned quantity 8 "ft"
        remark
            Combined with ALT_SIGN into a single signed value.
            The source of the data is given by the FOM/SOURCE field of
            BDS 5,2.
